{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/468871-2e-updating-the-rockies","id":468871,"title":"[2E] Updating The Rockies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-04T15:32:23-07:00","id":468871,"title":"[2E] Updating The Rockies","content":"Hi! Looking at the many changes brought up by the current edition, does any of you have made a list of things to change and/or replace with the Rockies supplement? I mean both in-setting and rules-wise.<br /> <br /> Does any of you came up with a different twist for the setting? I'd love to read what others have come up with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T16:39:37-07:00","id":468942,"title":"","content":"*enthusiastically subscribes to thread*<br /> <br /> (I'm a Coloradan and I've always adored the Hunting Grounds: the Rockies setting, even when I wasn't a big fan of 1e Forsaken)<br /> <br /> The first thing that comes to mind is the obvious need to update the NPCs character sheets (which I am in the process of doing, and I'd be happy to post when I finish if there is interest). Everyone's Harmony levels, Gifts, and Rites need to be completely re-done. Merits need some tweaking, since some no longer exist and new ones have been added. The Totem rules are a little bit different now, so they'll have to be adjusted. I really like the idea of Argent Peregrine granting the Silver Syndicate members a few dots in the new Falconry Merit from Hurt Locker, but I hesitate since that's still in draft stages. New Hope will probably need to find a Totem, since a dot of the Totem Merit is now free at character creation. The local packs may need to be expanded to include human and Wolf-Blooded members (except the Red Knives, who interestingly already worked that way, though it was considered unusual back then). I wonder if Black Moon Extreme might work better as Iron Masters now, since they essentially treated vampires as their sacred prey before, and that now falls under the <i>Farsil Luhal's </i>purview. Or maybe they're a tiny lodge? I don't know, still mulling that one over.<br /> <br /> Could be fun to think about how current events would have affected the setting. Maybe the legalization of Marajuana has given the smiling god up in Boulder a tremendous new source of happiness-infused essence? (speaking of which, now that <i>Welcome to Night Vale</i> is a thing, I really want to find a way to make the situation in Boulder a reference to Desert Bluffs). The Aurora theater shooting probably messed up the shadowscape in Aurora big time, maybe even created a wound? Just kind of throwing things out there, can't wait to hear other people's ideas though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-04-2015, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T22:10:11-07:00","id":469870,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/406618-max-roman-and-colorado-rockies-protectorate-failure\">You maybe interested also in this real life event in Colorado</a>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T00:15:36-07:00","id":469942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/468871-2e-updating-the-rockies?p=469870#post469870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/406618-max-roman-and-colorado-rockies-protectorate-failure\">You maybe interested also in this real life event in Colorado</a>...</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure. Personally, I run my games as &quot;like real life, except where the setting contradicts reality.&quot; So in my alternate version of Colorado, The Well's Fargo building in downtown Denver is owned by the Silver Syndicate instead of Well's Fargo, and it's called the Argentum building. The Pearl Street bookstore in Boulder is called the Nevermore bookstore, and efforts to reintroduce wolves into the area have been largely successful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T03:46:05-07:00","id":471073,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin, anything you care to share I'll be glad to read, truly.<br /> <br /> I think the most striking difference from the original material is the fact that packs include wolf-blooded and humans, now, and that tribes have a favored prey they hunt above all else. These changes open up possibilities in terms of pack composition, interpersonal drama and story complexity that I'm most intrigued to try out. For example, the Scar Angels seem like a real biker gang, now. And even that is not mandatory; the Three Sisters could just be the three Uratha, or they could include a few employees from their bookstore, or any other combination, really.<br /> <br /> If I were to change anything, it will be BMX's tribal composition, in that I agree completely with you. Almost 7-8 years passed since the book came out, so I imagine there must be a lot of real-world changes, which is something I'm not really familiar since I'm not a local. I'd love to read more about it.<br /> <br /> Also, for some time now I've started to search for real pictures of actors/actresses, models and other celebrities to replace their character portraits. I've found this really brings home a sense of reality and helps me and my players to remember the cast of characters, especially recurring NPCs. Have you ever tried that? Do you have any suggestions for the Uratha of Colorado?. I think sir Anthony Hopkins would do a terrifying Obadiah Pickering, but I feel he's too well known for it to work. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T09:49:51-07:00","id":471345,"title":"","content":"I'll gladly post my versions of the character sheets once I finish them. I'm currently waiting for the updated sheets though, cause I know Mr. Gone has made a few changes.<br /> <br /> I'm planning to use the pack creation rules pretty much as-written to add Wolf Blooded and human characters to each pack - one Wolf Blooded and two humans for each werewolf pack member (that's not <i>necessarily</i> the whole pack, just the ones that will come up in the story) using the simplified stats.<br /> <br /> Big setting changes in light of significant real world events since the book was written will be quite an undertaking since so much time has passed. I'm more focused on just updating the characters for now, but that will be my next step.<br /> <br /> Finding actors to play the NPCs is a neat idea. It's not something I've ever done, but I could give it some thought, for sure. Anthony Hopkins is a perfect Obediah!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}